\title{stepwedgepower: Simulation-Based Power Evaluation for Stepped-Wedge Trials}
\description{
Provides design objects, binary-outcome data generation, mixed-model
analysis, simulation-based power and type I error evaluation, sensitivity
grids, and validation tools for stepped-wedge cluster randomized trials.
The package supports asynchronous cumulative-intervention schedules and a
general component-based engine for Control, A, B, and A+B. The component
engine permits arbitrary withdrawal and reintroduction schedules,
structurally unobserved cluster-periods, wash-in, user-defined carryover decay, an A-by-B interaction, estimability audits,
multiplicity-aware contrasts, and failure-aware operating characteristics.
